=== 2026-10-31 · early-childhood-educator · Pace, tolerance and feedback for «كَيْفَ أَكْتُبُ؟» (acting via frontend-engineer, lead) ===
Lead / asked by: frontend-engineer (game lead)
Files reviewed: games/write.js, games/write.html, Playwright runs at 1280 / 820×1180 / 390
Findings:
  [MINOR] [ATTENTION] bint has 8 steps, hathihi 7 — long for KG — fix: they sit in level 3 only; level 1 letters are 1–4 steps
  [MINOR] [MOTOR] canvas cannot be used by keyboard/switch — fix: watch mode + Noori's help after three tries keeps every child moving to the stars
Decisions / judgement calls:
  - Pace: body 1.5–2.5 s, dot 0.8 s, haraka 1.1 s, 0.6 s pause; slower ×0.6 / faster ×1.5 — why: brief range; slow enough to follow with a finger
  - Tolerance: start within 40 units of the dot, ≥70 % of the child's line within 28 units, ≥70 % of the model covered, direction 75 % forward; ×1.2 per try up to ×1.6 — generous at iPad scale (~45–50 px)
  - Miss: line fades, Noori "thinks", one short hint («اِبْدَأْ مِنَ النُّقْطَةِ الْخَضْرَاءِ.» etc.), that stroke replays; never "wrong", no bad tone; 3rd miss → «سَأُسَاعِدُكَ» and Noori draws it
  - Reward: always 3 stars + confetti 40 + cheer at the end of an item; no score, no timer, nothing saved
Fixed this run:
  - Hint text cut to the hint only (was hint + full step phrase, too much to read) — verified in write-hint-hatha-t.png
Still open:
  - KG cut of the game (level 1 only, bigger stage) — owner: ceo scope
Notes for next time:
  - Test with a real 5–6-year-old on an iPad: is 28-unit tolerance too strict for a finger on the ب bowl?
[DONE]
